<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῐγῠρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
			Boeot.
		 fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγουρά</span></b>  (q.v.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clear, shrill</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦρτο δὲ κῦμα πνοιῇ ὕπο λιγυρῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.215
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.526
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.590
			</span></i>; of a whip, <i><span class="en">
				11.532
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				242
			</span></i> (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκόνα</span> (v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκόνη</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">;
				λιγυρὰ ἄχεα</span> griefs <i>which vent themselves in
				shrill wailings</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				205
			</span></i> (lyr.); also (like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγύς</span>),
			of a <i>clear, sweet</i> sound, as of the Sirens, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγυρῇ θέλγουσιν ἀοιδῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.44
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγυρὴν ἔντυνον ἀοιδήν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				183
			</span></i>; of a bird, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.290
			</span></i>; of locusts, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				583
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. σύριγγες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					278
				</span></i>
			: metaph., of poets, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Op.</u>
				659
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀοιδά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					15.135
				</span></i>
			, etc.: neut. pl. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγυρὰ ἀείδειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					939
				</span></i>
			: regul. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ρῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					8.71
				</span></i>
			.—Poet. word, used occasionally in Prose, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγυρὸν ὑπηχεῖ</span> echoes
			<i>shrilly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				230c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνὴ λ.</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμπρά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				616b31
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aud.</u>
				804a29
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			): also in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.974a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Salt.</u>
				72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phal.</u>
				1.11
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμβιῶναι . . ἥδιστος καὶ -ώτατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					4.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pliant, flexible</i>, of dogs' tails, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				4.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
